Shortest Path Visiting All Nodes (Hard – Bitmask + BFS)
📌 Problem Statement

You are given an undirected connected graph with n nodes labeled 0 to n-1.

You can:

Start at any node.

Visit nodes in any order.

Revisit nodes if needed.

Return the length of the shortest path that visits ALL nodes at least once.

🧾 Example
Input:
graph = [[1,2,3],[0],[0],[0]]

Output:
4


Graph:

     1
     |
2 — 0 — 3


One shortest path:

1 → 0 → 2 → 0 → 3


Length = 4

🧠 WHY BITMASK?

We must:

Track which nodes visited

Minimize path length

We use:

mask = binary number representing visited nodes


Example (n=4):

Visited nodes 0,2
mask = 0101 (binary) = 5


When:

mask == (1<<n) - 1


All nodes visited 🎯

💡 KEY IDEA

State in BFS:

(node, visited_mask)


This is NOT normal BFS.

We must track:

Current node

Which nodes visited so far

🪜 ALGORITHM
Step 1:

Initialize BFS queue.

Push all nodes as starting point:

(node i, mask with only node i visited)

Step 2:

Maintain visited[][] to avoid repeating states

visited[node][mask]

Step 3:

Run BFS

For each neighbor:

newMask = mask | (1 << neighbor)

Step 4:

If mask == fullMask → return steps

💻 FULL JAVA CODE
import java.util.*;

public class ShortestPathVisitingAllNodes {

    public static int shortestPathLength(int[][] graph) {

        int n = graph.length;

        int fullMask = (1 << n) - 1;

        Queue<int[]> queue = new LinkedList<>();

        boolean[][] visited = new boolean[n][1 << n];

        // Step 1: Initialize queue with all nodes
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int mask = (1 << i);
            queue.offer(new int[]{i, mask});
            visited[i][mask] = true;
        }

        int steps = 0;

        // Step 2: BFS
        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {

            int size = queue.size();

            for (int s = 0; s < size; s++) {

                int[] current = queue.poll();

                int node = current[0];
                int mask = current[1];

                // Step 3: If all nodes visited
                if (mask == fullMask) {
                    return steps;
                }

                // Explore neighbors
                for (int neighbor : graph[node]) {

                    int newMask = mask | (1 << neighbor);

                    if (!visited[neighbor][newMask]) {
                        visited[neighbor][newMask] = true;
                        queue.offer(new int[]{neighbor, newMask});
                    }
                }
            }

            steps++;
        }

        return -1;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[][] graph = {{1,2,3},{0},{0},{0}};

        System.out.println(shortestPathLength(graph));
    }
}

