⏳ TIME COMPLEXITY

There are:

n × 2^n states


Each state processes neighbors.

Time =

O(n × 2^n)


Works because n ≤ 12 (constraint).

🧠 INTERVIEW EXPLANATION

"This is a state-compression BFS problem. Since we must track visited nodes and revisit is allowed, I used a bitmask to represent visited nodes. Each BFS state consists of (currentNode, visitedMask). When the mask equals the full bitmask, we return the number of steps. Complexity is O(n × 2^n)."
